  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Hot, humid conditions persist into next week, \nalong with daily chances for shower and thunderstorms.\n\nThe Bermuda High remains in place across the western Atlantic into \nnext week. PWATS will be near or greater than 2\" in the valleys with \n1-2\" in the mountains. South to southwesterly flow is maintained \nover the Mid-Atlantic. Hot and humid conditions each afternoon, with \nhighs reaching the upper 80s to low 90s, and heat indices in the low \n100s each of the Blue Ridge. \n\nA surface trough is progged to remain over the area through Friday. \nAloft, pieces of shortwave energy continue passing overhead and help \ntrigger scattered showers and thunderstorms each afternoon. Deep \nlayer shear is forecast to increase through the weekend as the \nsubtropical jet stream strengthens. Hotter conditions may cause \nrelatively steeper low-level lapse rates and the wind field \nstrengthens a bit (especially Friday). This is going to bring an \nincreasing chance for strong to severe thunderstorms each day, with \nFriday and Saturday looking to have the highest chances. On \nSaturday, a more potent shortwave trough is forecast to move \noverhead that could aid in stronger, more organized severe \nconvection. Damaging wind gusts will be the main threat.\n\nA quasi-zonal flow aloft will develop Sunday into into next week. \nSunday could bring a short reprieve as dry conditions prevail. \nSeasonably hot, humid conditions along with daily chances for \nshowers and thunderstorms return Monday through most of next\nweek.",
